    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(Prerequisite: Ravenloft Campaign)</em></p><p>A cacophony of whispering spirits haunts you, and only you can hear them. You gain the following features.</p><p><strong>Spirit Whispers.</strong> You learn the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMessage000]{Message} cantrip, and you can cast it without Material components. @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplAugury0000]{Augury} is also always prepared for you: you can cast it without a spell slot or components, and you must finish a Long Rest before you can cast it this way again; you can also cast it with any spell slots you have. Your spellcasting ability for these spells is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (chosen when you take this feat).</p><p><strong>Unearthly Scream.</strong> When an attack roll hits you, you can take a Reaction to channel your spirits into a protective, otherworldly scream: add your Proficiency Bonus to your AC against that attack, which can make it miss. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Voices from Beyond.</strong> Immediately after you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, the whispers rise to a deafening roar. Make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 13 plus your Proficiency Bonus). On a failure, you have the &amp;Reference[Deafened] condition until the end of your next turn; while Deafened this way, you have Disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-AoIPRmTLK3OSzn0E\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Message and Augury are added by the feat; leave out the components yourself when you cast them through it. <em>Unearthly Scream</em> spends a use of the feat. <em>Voices from Beyond</em> is a Wisdom saving throw against DC 13 + your Proficiency Bonus; on a failure, apply its effect (Deafened).</p></section>",
